  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -36,
        -30
      ],
      "id": 29,
      "text": "ATmega8A at 1 MHz running avr_station, a student project in small: a 1 ms tick from Timer1 reads the\npotentiometer on ADC0 every 10 ms, sets the PWM on OC2 (PB3, 3.9 kHz) from it, blinks the LED on PB0\nevery 500 ms and reports over the USART every 100 ms. Drag RV1 while running: the PWM's duty and the\nfiltered voltage (R2, C1) follow, and the terminal shows the readings."
    }
  ],
